<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  robotiq_hande_module.urdf.xacro

  The Robotiq Hand-E as a module of a work cell. It wraps the vanilla
  robotiq_description macro (Robotiq's robotiq-ros, never edit that package,
  see third_party/vendored.yaml) and adds what a cell needs on top of it

  1. The UR coupling between the flange and the gripper, 11 mm. Robotiq's
     macro starts at the gripper's own base. 11 mm is measured by matching
     the housing of Robotiq's mesh to the robocoop cell's CAD of its
     assembly, which includes the coupling (mean profile error 0.19 mm, see
     modules/robotiq_hande.yaml).

  2. The module's borders (border.urdf.xacro), instance_mount on parent and
     the TCP instance_tcp on it, with the offset from
     modules/robotiq_hande.yaml (pad centre, 145 mm from the mount).
     Robotiq's macro has its own tcp_link 1.5 mm higher; skills use
     gripper_tcp.

  3. With sim_gazebo, a mass for each finger. The vanilla finger links have no
     inertial block, and the URDF to SDF conversion drops a massless link
     together with its joint, so Gazebo had no fingers and gz_ros2_control
     crashed writing to the missing joint (segfault in GazeboSimSystem write,
     Oct 2026). Each finger gets a child link with 30 g (a guess, the
     datasheet gives only the gripper's 1 kg) on a fixed joint, which the
     conversion lumps into the finger. Planning descriptions leave it out.

  4. With contact_pads, simulation-only pads, as the 2F-85 module has them.
     bullet-featherstone collides a mesh as its convex hull, and the Hand-E's
     finger mesh is an L, the slider inside the body reaching 34 mm inward
     above the pad. Its hull filled the space between pad and slider; open,
     it reached 4 mm into a 40 mm brick and pushed it away on the approach,
     and closing, the two hulls met with the fingers 1.3 mm in (Oct 2026). So
     each finger's mesh collides with nothing in Gazebo, and two boxes of its
     own carry the collisions, measured on the finger mesh (finger frame, the
     inner side towards the other finger) the gripping pad, 6 mm thick from
     the inner face at x 0, 21 mm wide, 23 to 47 mm down, and the finger body
     above it, stepped back 6 to 10.8 mm, 3 to 23 mm down. A link of its own
     on a fixed joint kept in Gazebo (preserveFixedJoint), since collision
     masks act per link in bullet-featherstone. Planning descriptions leave
     them out, FCL uses the meshes as they are.

  5. With sim_gazebo and include_ros2_control, the gripper's ros2_control
     block comes from this module, not from the vanilla macro: the vanilla
     block's Gazebo variant with the finger's command limits off, as the
     2F-85 module does and for the same reason. Since Lyrical the controller
     manager clamps a position command to one control period at the URDF
     velocity limit ahead of the finger, 0.15 mm at 0.075 m per s and 500 Hz;
     the fingers crept, an empty close stalled at 7 mm of the 50 mm stroke
     and an open timed out 3.5 mm short (Oct 2026). Gazebo still holds the
     joint inside its URDF limits. Under bullet-featherstone the right
     finger is left out of the block, the engine's mimic constraint alone
     moves it (see the block). With drive_mimic_finger (dartsim, which has
     no mimic constraints) it is listed, and gz_ros2_control drives it after
     the left one, as it drives the 2F-85's mimic joints on the gantry.

  6. For dartsim, as the 2F-85 module on the gantry (the reasoning is there,
     3. and 4.). With raise_finger_velocity_limits both fingers get 1 m per s
     as their velocity limit in the physics engine
     (cell_description.gz_joint_velocity_limits), the URDF's 0.075 stays.
     dartsim drops a joint's velocity command, which is how gz_ros2_control
     drives it, while the joint is at its velocity limit, and the finger then
     coasts; the gripper's speed comes from sim_gripper_driver's ramp. It
     also drops it at a position limit, and the Hand-E is commanded to
     exactly its URDF limits, 0 and 0.025, so the engine's position limits
     are widened by 2 mm each way. Without that a finger opened or closed
     fully stayed there, and the right finger, starting at 0, never followed
     the left one (Oct 2026). With
     contact_compliance a spring between the flange and the coupling, along
     the flange's z (robotiq_compliance_joint, prismatic, passive, a
     state-only ros2_control joint), 50 kN per m, damped near critical for
     the 1.03 kg on it (coupling, gripper, fingers), its rest position offset
     by that weight's sag. dartsim contacts are rigid, and force mode against
     a surface without it jumps between nothing and the arm's effort limits.
     The spring is the shared gripper_compliance macro
     (gripper_compliance.urdf.xacro, the reasoning is there). The TCP stays on
     the flange. Planning descriptions leave all of it off.

  The fingers are the vanilla macro's two prismatic joints (the right one
  mimics the left), 0 open to 0.025 closed per finger. Where /joint_states
  does not carry them, the planning scene holds them at 0, fully open, the
  widest footprint, as for the 2F-85's knuckle.

  Parameters, the same names as robotiq_2f_85_module's
    prefix                 link name prefix
    parent                 the output border the module's mount hangs on
                           (tool0 on a UR)
    instance               the module's name in the cell, the borders' prefix
                           (gripper gives gripper_mount and gripper_tcp)
    name                   ros2_control system name of the gripper
    include_ros2_control   with sim_gazebo, the module's own block (5.),
                           otherwise passed to the vanilla macro (its driver
                           talks to the gripper over RS-485, com_port)
    com_port               passed to the vanilla macro
    sim_gazebo             passed to the vanilla macro; also the finger masses
                           (3.)
    contact_pads           the simulation-only pads (4.)
    contact_compliance     the simulation-only wrist spring (6.)
    drive_mimic_finger     with the module's own Gazebo block, list the right
                           finger (5.); default false, under bullet-featherstone
                           listing it made the two fight, under dartsim it is
                           needed
    raise_finger_velocity_limits
                           in Gazebo, raise the fingers' velocity limits and
                           widen their position limits (6.)
  No pad_compliance, the 2F-85 module's yielding rubber layers (and with them
  sim_gripper_driver's force-limited grip); grasps on robocoop did not need it.

  Keep comments here free of colons (launch_ros reads robot_description as
  YAML first).
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <xacro:include filename="$(find robotiq_description)/urdf/robotiq_hand_e_macro.urdf.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find cell_description)/urdf/gripper_compliance.urdf.xacro"/>
  <xacro:include filename="$(find cell_description)/urdf/border.urdf.xacro"/>

  <!-- Two steps, see robotiq_2f_85_module.urdf.xacro. -->
  <xacro:property name="robotiq_hande_module_file" value="$(find cell_description)/modules/robotiq_hande.yaml"/>
  <xacro:property name="robotiq_hande_module_cfg" value="${xacro.load_yaml(robotiq_hande_module_file)}"/>

  <!-- See 1. above. Round, the gripper's 75 mm. -->
  <xacro:property name="robotiq_hande_coupling_length" value="0.011"/>
  <xacro:property name="robotiq_hande_coupling_radius" value="0.0375"/>

  <!-- See 4. above. inward is +1 for the left finger, whose inner side is +x,
       and -1 for the right one. -->
  <xacro:property name="robotiq_hande_pad_mu" value="0.8"/>
  <xacro:macro name="robotiq_hande_contact_pad" params="prefix side inward">
    <link name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_link">
      <inertial>
        <mass value="0.005"/>
        <inertia ixx="1e-6" iyy="1e-6" izz="1e-6" ixy="0" ixz="0" iyz="0"/>
      </inertial>
      <!-- Unnamed, sdformat calls them link_collision and _collision_1. -->
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="${-inward * 0.003} 0 0.035" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.006 0.021 0.024"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="${-inward * 0.0084} 0 0.013" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.0048 0.021 0.020"/></geometry>
      </collision>
    </link>
    <joint name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger"/>
      <child link="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_link"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
    <gazebo reference="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_joint">
      <preserveFixedJoint>true</preserveFixedJoint>
    </gazebo>
    <gazebo reference="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_link">
      <xacro:property name="mu" value="${robotiq_hande_pad_mu}"/>
      <collision name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_link_collision">
        <surface><friction><ode><mu>${mu}</mu><mu2>${mu}</mu2></ode><bullet><friction>${mu}</friction><friction2>${mu}</friction2></bullet></friction></surface>
      </collision>
      <collision name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_pad_link_collision_1">
        <surface><friction><ode><mu>${mu}</mu><mu2>${mu}</mu2></ode><bullet><friction>${mu}</friction><friction2>${mu}</friction2></bullet></friction></surface>
      </collision>
    </gazebo>
    <gazebo reference="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger">
      <collision name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_collision">
        <surface><contact><collide_bitmask>0x00</collide_bitmask></contact></surface>
      </collision>
    </gazebo>
  </xacro:macro>

  <!-- See 6. above. The mass on the spring (coupling 0.1, gripper 0.864,
       fingers and pads 0.07) for its rest offset. -->
  <xacro:property name="robotiq_hande_compliance_mass" value="1.034"/>

  <!-- See 5. above. -->
  <xacro:macro name="robotiq_hande_gazebo_ros2_control" params="name prefix drive_mimic:=false compliance:=false">
    <ros2_control name="${name}" type="system">
      <hardware>
        <plugin>gz_ros2_control/GazeboSimSystem</plugin>
      </hardware>
      <joint name="${prefix}hande_left_finger_joint">
        <limits enable="false"/>
        <command_interface name="position"/>
        <state_interface name="position">
          <param name="initial_value">0.0</param>
        </state_interface>
        <state_interface name="velocity"/>
      </joint>
      <!-- Under bullet-featherstone the right finger is not listed. It mimics
           the left one in the URDF, which bullet-featherstone turns into a
           constraint; listed here as well, gz_ros2_control drove it too, and
           the two fought, the fingers crawling at 0.5 mm per s (the 2F-85's
           revolute mimic joints do not show this). dartsim has no mimic
           constraints, so there it is listed and gz_ros2_control drives it. -->
      <xacro:if value="${drive_mimic}">
        <joint name="${prefix}hande_right_finger_joint"/>
      </xacro:if>
      <xacro:if value="${compliance}">
        <!-- Passive, see 6. above. State only, so TF follows the spring. -->
        <xacro:gripper_compliance_state_joint prefix="${prefix}"/>
      </xacro:if>
    </ros2_control>
  </xacro:macro>

  <!-- See 3. above. -->
  <xacro:macro name="robotiq_hande_finger_mass" params="prefix side">
    <link name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_mass">
      <inertial>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0.02" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <mass value="0.03"/>
        <inertia ixx="5e-6" iyy="5e-6" izz="2e-6" ixy="0" ixz="0" iyz="0"/>
      </inertial>
    </link>
    <joint name="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_mass_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger"/>
      <child link="${prefix}hande_${side}_finger_mass"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>

  <xacro:macro name="robotiq_hande_module"
               params="prefix:='' parent instance:=gripper name:=RobotiqGripperHardwareInterface include_ros2_control:=false
                       com_port:=/dev/ttyUSB0 sim_gazebo:=false contact_pads:=false
                       contact_compliance:=false
                       drive_mimic_finger:=false raise_finger_velocity_limits:=false">
    <xacro:property name="frames" value="${robotiq_hande_module_cfg['frames']}"/>
    <xacro:property name="mount" value="${prefix}${instance}${frames['mount']}"/>
    <xacro:border name="${mount}" parent="${parent}"/>
    <xacro:property name="coupling_parent" value="${mount}"/>
    <xacro:if value="${contact_compliance}">
      <xacro:gripper_compliance prefix="${prefix}" parent="${mount}" mass="${robotiq_hande_compliance_mass}"/>
      <xacro:property name="coupling_parent" value="${prefix}robotiq_compliance_link"/>
    </xacro:if>
    <link name="${prefix}robotiq_hande_coupling_link">
      <visual>
        <origin xyz="0 0 ${robotiq_hande_coupling_length / 2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder radius="${robotiq_hande_coupling_radius}" length="${robotiq_hande_coupling_length}"/>
        </geometry>
        <material name="robotiq_hande_coupling_grey">
          <color rgba="0.3 0.3 0.3 1.0"/>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <collision>
        <origin xyz="0 0 ${robotiq_hande_coupling_length / 2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder radius="${robotiq_hande_coupling_radius}" length="${robotiq_hande_coupling_length}"/>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
      <inertial>
        <origin xyz="0 0 ${robotiq_hande_coupling_length / 2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <mass value="0.1"/>
        <inertia ixx="4e-5" iyy="4e-5" izz="7e-5" ixy="0" ixz="0" iyz="0"/>
      </inertial>
    </link>
    <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_hande_coupling_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${coupling_parent}"/>
      <child link="${prefix}robotiq_hande_coupling_link"/>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </joint>

    <xacro:property name="own_ros2_control" value="${sim_gazebo and include_ros2_control}"/>
    <xacro:robotiq_gripper
        name="${name}"
        prefix="${prefix}"
        parent="${prefix}robotiq_hande_coupling_link"
        include_ros2_control="${include_ros2_control and not own_ros2_control}"
        sim_gazebo="${sim_gazebo}"
        com_port="${com_port}">
      <origin xyz="0 0 ${robotiq_hande_coupling_length}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    </xacro:robotiq_gripper>

    <xacro:if value="${own_ros2_control}">
      <xacro:robotiq_hande_gazebo_ros2_control name="${name}" prefix="${prefix}"
                                               drive_mimic="${drive_mimic_finger}"
                                               compliance="${contact_compliance}"/>
      <!-- See 6. above. -->
      <xacro:if value="${raise_finger_velocity_limits}">
        <gazebo>
          <plugin filename="gz-sim-python-system-loader-system" name="gz::sim::systems::PythonSystemLoader">
            <module_name>cell_description.gz_joint_velocity_limits</module_name>
            <joints>${prefix}hande_left_finger_joint ${prefix}hande_right_finger_joint</joints>
            <velocity>1.0</velocity>
            <position_limits>-0.002 0.027</position_limits>
          </plugin>
        </gazebo>
      </xacro:if>
    </xacro:if>
    <xacro:if value="${sim_gazebo}">
      <xacro:robotiq_hande_finger_mass prefix="${prefix}" side="left"/>
      <xacro:robotiq_hande_finger_mass prefix="${prefix}" side="right"/>
    </xacro:if>
    <xacro:if value="${contact_pads}">
      <xacro:robotiq_hande_contact_pad prefix="${prefix}" side="left" inward="1"/>
      <xacro:robotiq_hande_contact_pad prefix="${prefix}" side="right" inward="-1"/>
    </xacro:if>

    <xacro:property name="tcp" value="${robotiq_hande_module_cfg['tcp']}"/>
    <xacro:property name="tcp_frame" value="${prefix}${instance}${frames['tcp']}"/>
    <link name="${tcp_frame}"/>
    <joint name="${tcp_frame}_joint" type="fixed">
      <parent link="${mount}"/>
      <child link="${tcp_frame}"/>
      <origin xyz="${tcp['xyz'][0]} ${tcp['xyz'][1]} ${tcp['xyz'][2]}"
              rpy="${tcp['rpy'][0]} ${tcp['rpy'][1]} ${tcp['rpy'][2]}"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
